{#
  The end of every page's Markdown: the archive on a page that asked for one,
  what the page is filed under, what links to it, a post's neighbours, the
  feeds, then a heading and the site's link lists.

  `archiveMonths` is on the context only of a page whose front matter says
  `archive: true`: every published post as `{ month, posts }`, newest month
  first. Each post is a `label`, a `url`, a `date` (`YYYY-MM-DD`) and a
  `description` already on one line, written here in the shape a listing's
  Markdown has.

  `categories` and `tags` are a post's, each a `label` (the term as written)
  and the `url` of its archive. `backlinks` are the site's posts and pages
  that link to this one, newest first, each a `label`, a `url` and a `date`.
  This theme leaves them off a homepage that is a page, as its front page
  layout does; a site theme may print them there.
  `feeds` are the feeds the HTML head advertises, each a `label` (the feed's
  title), a `url`, a `format` (`RSS`, `Atom` or `JSON Feed`) and a `type`.
  `type` is `post`, `page` or `listing`; a listing's newer and older pages
  are written by the CMS above this, so only a post's `previous` and `next`
  are printed here.

  `byline` is a post's author, a `label` and the `url` of their archive.
  `navigation` is every item of every menu the site stores, each URL once,
  each a `label` and a `url`; `menus` has them by menu name, as the HTML
  does. `home`, `previous` and `next` are here too; the front matter carries
  them as well, for a Markdown browser.

  Each link is a line of its own, with its own words, so the same data can be
  written as a Gemini link line. Nothing is printed when there is nothing to
  link.
#}
{% for group in archiveMonths %}
## {{ group.month | escapeMarkdown }}

{% for entry in group.posts %}
- [{{ (((entry.date + " ") if entry.date) + entry.label) | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ entry.url | markdownUrl }}){{ (": " + entry.description) if entry.description }}
{% endfor %}

{% endfor %}
{% if categories.length or tags.length %}
## Filed under

{% for link in categories %}
- [Category: {{ link.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ link.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endfor %}
{% for link in tags %}
- [Tag: {{ link.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ link.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if backlinks.length and not staticFrontPage %}
## Linked from

{% for entry in backlinks %}
- [{{ (((entry.date + " ") if entry.date) + entry.label) | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ entry.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if type == "post" and (previous or next) %}
## More posts

{% if previous %}
- [Previous: {{ previous.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ previous.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endif %}
{% if next %}
- [Next: {{ next.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ next.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endif %}

{% endif %}
{% if feeds.length %}
## Feeds

{% for feed in feeds %}
- [{{ (feed.label + " (" + feed.format + ")") | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ feed.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if byline or navigation.length %}
## {{ site.title | escapeMarkdown }}

{% if byline %}
[Written by {{ byline.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ byline.url | markdownUrl }})

{% endif %}
{% for item in navigation %}
- [{{ item.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ item.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
